Don't Blink — a Pixel Countdown Science film · credits & licences

ORIGINAL (made for this film, by code in this folder)
- All pixel art: the eye, lids and lashes, the tear-drop character, the TEAR FILM gauge, the ground (eye.js, scene.js, main.js).
- Captions and counters (font.js). Music and sound effects synthesised with numpy (groove.py, mix.py); the end melody is original.

CODE ADAPTED FROM LEMO-OPUSCAR (MIT licence, github.com/lemomo-ai/lemo-opuscar)
- px.js and the 5×7 glyph table in font.js (from styles/pixel-rpg/demo); sound helpers from core/audio/sfx.py.

PALETTE
- ENDESGA 32 by ENDESGA (lospec.com/palette-list/endesga-32), plus custom ground/yellow tones.

FACTS (see TREATMENT.md for the sources)
- Blink rate ~15–20/min; tear film breaks up after ~10 s; ~1 h/day with eyes shut by blinks (estimate);
  blink suppression in the brain; ~22/min relaxed vs ~7/min at a screen (Tsubota & Nakamori, NEJM 1993).

No third-party images, fonts, samples or recordings. No voice.
